WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.245
Lesson 3.2.

00:00:02.245 --> 00:00:05.855
LTV, liquidation threshold, and health factor.

00:00:05.855 --> 00:00:08.285
These three numbers decide whether a loan

00:00:08.285 --> 00:00:09.500
is a tool, or a trap.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.165
Here's the uncomfortable truth about borrowing on-chain.

00:00:14.165 --> 00:00:16.640
A lending protocol never calls you.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.290
There's no margin call, no grace period,

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.465
and no one to negotiate with.

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:23.477
When your collateral falls too far,

00:00:23.477 --> 00:00:25.900
it's sold automatically, at a penalty.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.865
So the only protection you have is

00:00:27.865 --> 00:00:30.055
arithmetic you did before you borrowed.

00:00:31.355 --> 00:00:33.052
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:33.052 --> 00:00:34.700
be able to do three things.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.290
Measure your loan-to-value and health factor for any position.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.625
Locate the exact price at which you'd be liquidated.

00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:44.466
And defend the position, by choosing a buffer and

00:00:44.466 --> 00:00:46.795
a plan before you borrow a single dollar.

00:00:48.095 --> 00:00:51.313
Every lending position comes down to four numbers.

00:00:51.313 --> 00:00:53.948
First, LTV, or loan-to-value.

00:00:53.948 --> 00:00:55.726
It's simply your debt divided by

00:00:55.726 --> 00:00:57.588
the value of your collateral.

00:00:57.588 --> 00:01:00.155
Second, max LTV. That's the most the

00:01:00.155 --> 00:01:03.368
protocol lets you borrow against an asset.

00:01:03.368 --> 00:01:05.683
Third, the liquidation threshold.

00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:08.960
That's the loan-to-value at which your position can

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.922
be liquidated, and it's always set higher than

00:01:11.922 --> 00:01:14.428
max LTV. Fourth, the health factor.

00:01:14.428 --> 00:01:16.956
Collateral value, times the liquidation

00:01:16.956 --> 00:01:18.978
threshold, divided by your debt.

00:01:20.278 --> 00:01:22.698
If you remember one thing, remember this.

00:01:22.698 --> 00:01:24.595
When the health factor falls below

00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:26.793
one, your position is liquidatable.

00:01:26.793 --> 00:01:28.658
Above one, you're safe, for now.

00:01:28.658 --> 00:01:30.516
At one or below, anyone can repay

00:01:30.516 --> 00:01:32.320
part of your debt, and take some

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.423
of your collateral at a discount.

00:01:34.423 --> 00:01:37.003
That discount is the penalty, and you pay it.

00:01:38.302 --> 00:01:39.425
People mix up the two

00:01:39.425 --> 00:01:41.307
limits, so let's separate them.

00:01:41.307 --> 00:01:44.082
Max LTV is a borrowing limit.

00:01:44.082 --> 00:01:46.084
It stops you taking on more debt, and

00:01:46.084 --> 00:01:47.912
on its own it can't hurt you.

00:01:47.912 --> 00:01:50.527
The liquidation threshold is a trigger.

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:52.777
Cross it, and liquidation starts.

00:01:52.777 --> 00:01:54.652
That's where you actually lose collateral.

00:01:55.952 --> 00:01:58.717
Let's work a real example, step by step.

00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:02.842
You deposit 10 ETH at $3,000 each.

00:02:02.842 --> 00:02:05.826
Your collateral is worth $30,000.

00:02:05.826 --> 00:02:08.916
You borrow $12,000 of stablecoins.

00:02:08.916 --> 00:02:12.996
Loan-to-value is $12,000 divided by $30,000.

00:02:12.996 --> 00:02:14.481
That's 40%.

00:02:14.481 --> 00:02:19.044
The liquidation threshold is 0.8, so the health

00:02:19.044 --> 00:02:22.576
factor is $30,000 × 0.8 ÷ $12,000.

00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:24.171
That's exactly 2.

00:02:24.171 --> 00:02:26.446
And the liquidation price is your debt

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.371
divided by your quantity times the threshold.

00:02:29.371 --> 00:02:31.841
$12,000 ÷ 8.

00:02:31.841 --> 00:02:33.756
That's $1,500.

00:02:33.756 --> 00:02:37.841
So ETH can fall 50% before you're liquidated.

00:02:39.141 --> 00:02:41.806
Now watch what happens as you borrow more.

00:02:41.806 --> 00:02:44.347
Aim for a health factor of 1.5,

00:02:44.347 --> 00:02:46.949
and your debt can be $16,000.

00:02:46.949 --> 00:02:50.284
Your liquidation price rises to $2,000.

00:02:50.284 --> 00:02:53.144
A 33% drop now liquidates you.

00:02:53.144 --> 00:02:56.292
Suppose, as an illustration, the market

00:02:56.292 --> 00:02:58.639
lets you borrow up to 75%.

00:02:58.639 --> 00:03:01.324
That's $22,500.

00:03:01.324 --> 00:03:06.494
The health factor is $24,000 ÷ $22,500.

00:03:06.494 --> 00:03:08.269
About 1.07.

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:12.954
Your liquidation price becomes $2,812.50.

00:03:12.954 --> 00:03:15.199
A drop of just over 6%.

00:03:15.199 --> 00:03:17.479
Crypto can move that much in an hour.

00:03:17.479 --> 00:03:20.134
Borrowing the maximum leaves almost no room.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.709
Here's the same story as a picture.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:26.632
The horizontal axis is the price of ETH.

00:03:26.632 --> 00:03:29.784
The vertical axis is your health factor.

00:03:29.784 --> 00:03:32.804
Start at today, $3,000, where the blue line

00:03:32.804 --> 00:03:35.094
sits at a health factor of 2.

00:03:35.094 --> 00:03:37.707
Follow the blue line down and left,

00:03:37.707 --> 00:03:39.967
and it crosses 1 at $1,500.

00:03:39.967 --> 00:03:41.902
That's your liquidation price.

00:03:41.902 --> 00:03:45.167
Now the orange line, with $16,000 of debt.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:48.677
It starts lower, and it hits 1 at $2,000.

00:03:48.677 --> 00:03:50.992
More debt doesn't just lower the line.

00:03:50.992 --> 00:03:52.046
It moves the cliff edge

00:03:52.046 --> 00:03:53.452
closer to where you're standing.

00:03:54.752 --> 00:03:55.937
And here's why the buffer

00:03:55.937 --> 00:03:57.467
matters more than it looks.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.832
Liquidations sell collateral into a falling market.

00:04:00.832 --> 00:04:03.144
That selling pushes the price lower, which

00:04:03.144 --> 00:04:05.487
triggers the next set of liquidations.

00:04:05.487 --> 00:04:06.607
A cascade.

00:04:06.607 --> 00:04:09.373
The move that reaches your liquidation price is

00:04:09.373 --> 00:04:12.267
often faster and deeper than anyone expected.

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.572
Your buffer is the time you have to react.

00:04:15.872 --> 00:04:17.619
When the health factor falls, you

00:04:17.619 --> 00:04:19.357
have three ways to raise it.

00:04:19.357 --> 00:04:20.542
Repay debt.

00:04:20.542 --> 00:04:22.193
That's the most direct fix, so

00:04:22.193 --> 00:04:24.357
keep some stablecoins ready for it.

00:04:24.357 --> 00:04:26.204
Add collateral, from a reserve you

00:04:26.204 --> 00:04:28.087
set aside before you borrowed.

00:04:28.087 --> 00:04:29.944
Or the cheapest defence of all:

00:04:29.944 --> 00:04:32.042
borrow less in the first place.

00:04:32.042 --> 00:04:34.485
Decide which lever you'll pull, and at what

00:04:34.485 --> 00:04:37.227
health factor, before you open the position.

00:04:37.227 --> 00:04:38.452
Not during the crash.

00:04:39.752 --> 00:04:42.247
Four mistakes cause most liquidations.

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:44.208
Borrowing right up to max LTV,

00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:46.342
because the button allows it.

00:04:46.342 --> 00:04:49.435
Forgetting that interest keeps growing the debt, so the

00:04:49.435 --> 00:04:52.717
health factor drifts down even when prices don't move.

00:04:52.717 --> 00:04:54.305
Having no alert, or an alert

00:04:54.305 --> 00:04:56.302
that fires while you're asleep.

00:04:56.302 --> 00:04:58.885
And having no reserve, so when the moment comes

00:04:58.885 --> 00:05:01.037
there's nothing to repay or top up with.

00:05:02.337 --> 00:05:04.472
Here's your checklist for this lesson.

00:05:04.472 --> 00:05:08.787
HF and liquidation price calculated before borrowing.

00:05:08.787 --> 00:05:10.032
A health factor of at

00:05:10.032 --> 00:05:12.142
least 2 for volatile collateral.

00:05:12.142 --> 00:05:14.033
And alerts set, which we

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.302
build properly in Module 14.1.

00:05:17.602 --> 00:05:18.812
Question one.

00:05:18.812 --> 00:05:23.206
Collateral is worth $50,000, the liquidation threshold

00:05:23.206 --> 00:05:26.062
is 0.8, and the debt is $20,000.

00:05:26.062 --> 00:05:27.347
What's the health factor?

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:33.252
The answer: 2.

00:05:33.252 --> 00:05:38.187
$50,000 × 0.8 is $40,000, divided by $20,000.

00:05:39.487 --> 00:05:40.732
Question two.

00:05:40.732 --> 00:05:42.777
Why keep the health factor well above 1?

00:05:47.197 --> 00:05:50.298
The answer: collateral prices can fall fast.

00:05:50.298 --> 00:05:52.113
The buffer is your time to react.

00:05:53.413 --> 00:05:54.683
Question three.

00:05:54.683 --> 00:05:56.856
What's the difference between max

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.028
LTV and the liquidation threshold?

00:06:03.448 --> 00:06:06.778
The answer: max LTV caps new borrowing.

00:06:06.778 --> 00:06:10.488
The liquidation threshold is where liquidation becomes possible.

00:06:11.788 --> 00:06:13.033
Let's recap.

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:15.958
A health factor below one means liquidatable.

00:06:15.958 --> 00:06:18.762
Your liquidation price is your debt, divided

00:06:18.762 --> 00:06:21.803
by quantity times the liquidation threshold.

00:06:21.803 --> 00:06:24.378
More debt moves the cliff closer, fast.

00:06:24.378 --> 00:06:26.115
And your buffer, and your plan,

00:06:26.115 --> 00:06:28.043
are decided before you borrow.

00:06:28.043 --> 00:06:29.348
Never during the crash.

00:06:30.648 --> 00:06:32.261
Do the checklist now, with the

00:06:32.261 --> 00:06:34.173
calculator, before you move on.

00:06:34.173 --> 00:06:36.968
Next up, Lesson 3.3: liquidations and

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:39.468
cascades, and how to survive them.
